 "_doc": "The scenic cities (sim/catalog/scenic.h, api/scenic_loader.cpp): cities laid out by hand, each on the map of data/catalog/maps.json that names it. Coordinates are metres [x, z] from the map's middle, x to the east and z to the south (north is -z). sao_paulo: a scenic Sao Paulo, not to scale and not a survey: the Tiete in the north and the Pinheiros in the west meeting at the north-west corner, the Tamanduatei in the east, Paulista on its ridge, the Centro, Jardins, Pinheiros and Faria Lima, Ibirapuera with its lake, the expressways along the rivers. land: the plateau at base_m rolling by relief_amp_m, ridges raised over it, rivers drawn downstream in their channels (level_start_m at the first point, level_end_m at the last), lakes sunk below_shore_m under the land of their shore. districts: each a street grid turned bearing_deg from +x, blocks [along, across], its own heat and trade; the square of city_half_m round the middle is split between their seeds (Voronoi), and seam streets run on the borders. roads: the plan's roads on their own line or on a river's course offset_m to its right bank (negative: the left), looking downstream; name_key: the name on its plates (data/i18n), none: one from the style's list. heat: density and trade laid along a line or round a point, fading to nothing at reach_m. zoning: dense over high_heat, medium over medium_heat, commercial over commerce_trade (main_trade beside a main road). trees: the parks' trees.",
